<title>USA: Boeing sees 1997 sales of $33 billion.</title>
<headline>Boeing sees 1997 sales of $33 billion.</headline>
<dateline>SEATTLE 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boeing Co said it expects 1997 sales in the $33 billion range on deliveries of 340 commercial jets, excluding the impact of its proposed merger with McDonnell Douglas Corp.</p>
<p>Boeing said in its earnings statement that the deliveries would include 60 777s as total monthly production rises to 40 aircraft in the fourth quarter from 22.5 currently.</p>
<p>Boeing previously said it expects 1997 sales of $48 billion, including McDonnell Douglas, assuming the transaction closes this summer as anticipated.</p>
</text>
